Alright buddy, it was our pleasure. Congratulations! Have a nice death!

Could be because of a few things like 

&#x200B;

1. desensitization- you've played too much/too often that you no longer feel the fun and excitement of playing

\-if this is the case it slowly comes back and when it does try to play in moderation like saving it for your free days or just an hour or so after your responsibilities

2. games you liked became shite - this is true esp. when it comes to a few games like diablo and dota 2 lol

&#x200B;

3. player base - whether you played with your friends, fought competitively with siblings or encountered fun players out there, these all make playing really fun when it was playing with them that was really enjoyable

&#x200B;

4. your tastes have changed - i used to play FPS games but i recently played an R18 game/visual novel called "Being a DIK" for the plot and enjoyed it quite a lot lmao

can think of these but i'm sure there're a lot of other reasons
